  "content": {
    "id": "p25-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "A sum of $\\$1500$ is invested at the end of each year for 15 years at 8% p.a.\nFind the amount of superannuation available at the end of the 15 years. Give your answer to the nearest cent.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\$40\\,728.17$",
      "worked": "End of 1st year: $1500$.\n\nEnd of 2nd year: $1500(1.08)+1500$.\n\nEnd of 15th year: $1500(1.08)^{14}+1500(1.08)^{13}+\\cdots+1500$.\n\nThis is a geometric series with $a=1500$, $r=1.08$ and $n=15$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}FV&=\\frac{a(r^n-1)}{r-1}\\\\FV&=\\frac{1500(1.08^{15}-1)}{1.08-1}\\\\FV&\\approx\\$40\\,728.17\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 50
  },
